      "card_ids": ["C02"],
      "claim": "A closely related N-methyl propargyl phenethylamine tracer shows high initial brain uptake (5.2 %ID/g) in mice, supporting efficient CNS entry for this chemotype.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C07"],
      "claim": "A benzylic tertiary amine radiotracer shows great brain uptake (0.8–1.4 %ID/g at 5 min) in rodents.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C16"],
      "claim": "BRL 44408, a related tricyclic-like amine, moderately crosses the BBB with a brain/plasma ratio of 0.51 in rats.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C04"],
      "claim": "Amphetamine, a small basic amine, readily crosses the BBB by passive diffusion with a BUI of 98% in rats, supporting that basic amines of this class can achieve CNS access.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query is a tricyclic tertiary amine with physicochemical properties favorable for passive BBB penetration. Multiple high-transfer experimental analogues, including direct brain uptake and brain/plasma measurements in rodents, consistently demonstrate meaningful CNS access. The experimental evidence strongly supports a pass prediction.",
